      "id": 12365,
      "name": "payprplayn",
      "username": "payprplayn",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/b2d939/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-21T01:43:01.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>If Visionary and her decoy projection are in the area of an area attack, can she have it take two hits and her none? &nbsp;It seems like the RAW you could, since area attacks hit each target in their area, not each hex. (The projection gets attacked, because it's in the area, and since the visionary is also in the area, she would be attacked, and therefore can switch with the projection to have it take the hit.) But thematically, it seems wrong. (She's either in one place or the other, and both places are in the blast.) &nbsp;So which is correct?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:52.784Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 6,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 30.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 12363,
      "topic_slug": "decoy-projection-and-area-attacks",
      "display_username": "payprplayn",
