      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Donner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/48/1903_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Donner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It's not a double-switcheroo.&nbsp; He takes his own hit, then he intercepts his ally's hit.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Agreed, with the minor pedanticism that it's up to the attacker to determine which targets defend in which order. Regardless, Legacy may defend for both by switching just once.</p>",
