      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Regardless, Legacy may defend for both by switching just once.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's what I thought. &nbsp;I'm not even going to bother putting that into the FAQ because Legacy isn't doing anything particularly special - he's just using Heroic Interception to save a friend once per attack like normal, with the slight oddity that he also had to take the attack for himself too because it was an area attack.</p>",
